{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "bronze_packing",
  "description": "a circle packing in bronze and gold: the frame filled with round discs of every size, each a flat metal disc with a dark bevel, a bright rim, a glint at its centre, faint rays and a packing of smaller beads inside, glints crowding the cusps where discs meet, and the set's own components gold star-flowers among them",
  "reference": {
    "image": "795549-3840x2160-desktop-4k-fractal-background.jpg",
    "folder": "fractal-drive-sync/style-refs",
    "made_with": "unknown; a Kleinian/inversion circle packing, 3840x2160 (a 4k desktop background, the sibling of teal_tunnel's reference)"
  },
  "suggested_colormap": "bronze_packing",
  "reuses": [
    "the style compositor, its palette, light, glow and sheet layers, warp, invert, and the normal, multiply, add and screen blends",
    "field smooth through the map by rank: the escaped field no disc caught",
    "the inside channel by rank at gamma 0.6: the set's components as gold flowers, their rings of convergence the petals",
    "the light layer at period 2 on the new bubble height: each disc a shallow dome (rings 0.4) with a Fresnel rim and a specular highlight",
    "the glow layer four times on the bubble height: a multiplied dark bevel inside each rim, the bright rim itself, a glint at each disc's centre, and the same rim and glint on the nested discs",
    "a glow on the entry step: the late, tiny discs that crowd every cusp, lit as sparkle",
    "a sheet on the entry angle at six bands: faint rays from each disc's centre",
    "the tone pass, at the reference's median and p10"
  ],
  "adds": [
    "channel bubble {center, radius, hit, read, spacing, escaped, largest}: the disc |z - center| < radius read at the step the orbit enters it for the hit-th time, its own loop with dz kept so the height has a gradient. The samples entering first at step n are a conformal preimage of the disc, so they draw round discs, and later steps fill the gaps: a circle packing. read is height (1 - |z - center|/radius, a dome a light at period 2 lights as a hemisphere), step (one number per disc) or angle (rays from each disc's middle); hit 2 is a packing of smaller discs inside each disc of hit 1; spacing repeats the disc on a square lattice so almost every orbit lands in one; escaped reads only escaping orbits, leaving the set's components to the inside channel; largest passes over an entry whose disc pulls back larger than that fraction of the frame width (radius / |dz| > largest * width), so the packing starts at a frame-relative size at any zoom depth"
  ],
